ShortDescription: Answers physics questions, from textbook to absurd, with small language models and a math engine, all on your own machine.
Description: |-
  Ask Physics answers physics questions in the terminal. Small language models written from
  scratch for this project (the Fermi family) classify the question, pick the equations and
  explain the result; Noether, a math engine built on SymPy and Pint, does every calculation
  and unit conversion, so the numbers are computed, not guessed. It runs locally, with no
  accounts and no API keys.

  The installer sets up uv (if needed) and installs the askphysics command in its own
  isolated Python environment for the current user, then downloads the Fermi models.
